Put coordinate axes on R³ so that the z-axis points vertically. 
Then a plane in R³ is vertical if its normal vector n is horizontal (id n is parallel to the xy-plane). 
This means that n has no k-conponent, so n can be written in the form Ai + Bj. 
It follows from equation 2 that a veritical plane has an equation of the form 

		A(x - x₀) + B(y - y₀) = 0

Hence, a nonvertical plane has an equation of the form 

		A(x - x0) + B(y - y0) + C(z - z₀) = 0

where C != 0
